```python
# main.py
FUNCTION register(username, password):
    OPEN 'users.txt' IN append+ mode
    FOR each line in file:
        IF username exists:
            RETURN False (username taken)
    GENERATE password_hash USING werkzeug.security.generate_password_hash(password)
    WRITE username|password_hash TO 'users.txt'
    RETURN True (registration successful)
END FUNCTION

# templates/register.html
<form method="POST" action="/register">
    <label>Username:</label>
    <input type="text" name="username" required>
    <label>Password:</label>
    <input type="password" name="password" required>
    <button type="submit">Register</button>
</form>
```
Key Libraries:  
- `werkzeug.security` for password hashing.

2. |Case|:user_login
```
FUNCTION login(username, password)  
    OPEN users.txt IN read mode  
    FOR each line IN users.txt  
        SPLIT line INTO parts[username, password]  
        IF parts[0] == username AND parts[1] == password  
            RETURN True  
    RETURN False  
END FUNCTION  

ROUTE /login (GET/POST)  
    IF POST request  
        CALL login(username, password)  
        IF successful  
            SET session['username'] = username  
            REDIRECT to dashboard  
        ELSE  
            RENDER login.html WITH error="Invalid credentials"  
    ELSE  
        RENDER login.html  
END ROUTE  
```
Key Libraries:  
- Flask for session and request handling.

