## Experience and Lessons
|Case|:book_search
```
FUNCTION search(query)  
    INITIALIZE results = []  
    OPEN books.txt IN read mode  
    FOR each line IN books.txt  
        SPLIT line INTO title, author, summary, description  
        IF query.lower() IN title.lower() OR query.lower() IN author.lower()  
            APPEND new Book(title, author, summary, description) to results  
    RETURN results  
END FUNCTION  

ROUTE /dashboard (GET/POST)  
    IF 'username' NOT IN session  
        REDIRECT to login  
    IF POST request  
        CALL search(query)  
        RENDER dashboard.html WITH books=results  
    ELSE  
        RENDER dashboard.html WITH books=[]  
END ROUTE  
```
Key Libraries:  
- Flask for request/response handling.

4. |Case|:view_book_details
```
FUNCTION get_book_details(title)  
    OPEN books.txt IN read mode  
    FOR each line IN books.txt  
        SPLIT line INTO title, author, summary, description  
        IF title == input_title  
            RETURN new Book(title, author, summary, description)  
    RETURN None  
END FUNCTION  

ROUTE /book/<title>  
    IF 'username' NOT IN session  
        REDIRECT to login  
    CALL get_book_details(title)  
    IF book exists  
        RENDER book_details.html WITH book  
    ELSE  
        REDIRECT to dashboard  
END ROUTE  
```
Key Libraries:  
- Flask for dynamic routing.

