## Experience and Lessons
|Case|:add_book_to_reading_list
```
FUNCTION add_to_list(username, book_title)  
    READ reading_lists.txt INTO dictionary lists  
    IF username NOT IN lists  
        SET lists[username] = []  
    IF book_title NOT IN lists[username]  
        APPEND book_title to lists[username]  
        WRITE lists back to reading_lists.txt  
        RETURN True  
    RETURN False  
END FUNCTION  

ROUTE /add_to_list/<title>  
    IF 'username' NOT IN session  
        REDIRECT to login  
    CALL add_to_list(session['username'], title)  
    REDIRECT to reading_list  
END ROUTE  
```
Key Libraries:  
- Flask for session management.

6. |Case|:view_and_manage_reading_list
```
FUNCTION get_list(username)  
    READ reading_lists.txt INTO dictionary lists  
    RETURN lists.get(username, [])  
END FUNCTION  

FUNCTION remove_from_list(username, book_title)  
    READ reading_lists.txt INTO dictionary lists  
    IF username IN lists AND book_title IN lists[username]  
        REMOVE book_title FROM lists[username]  
        WRITE lists back to reading_lists.txt  
        RETURN True  
    RETURN False  
END FUNCTION  

ROUTE /reading_list  
    IF 'username' NOT IN session  
        REDIRECT to login  
    CALL get_list(session['username'])  
    FOR each title IN list  
        CALL get_book_details(title)  
        APPEND book to books[]  
    RENDER reading_list.html WITH books  
END ROUTE  

ROUTE /remove_from_list/<title>  
    IF 'username' NOT IN session  
        REDIRECT to login  
    CALL remove_from_list(session['username'], title)  
    REDIRECT to reading_list  
END ROUTE  
```
Key Libraries:  
- Flask for session and routing.

